<article class="env-lemma" id="05EF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05EF">Lemma <span data-tag="05EF">15.91.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $I = (f_1, \ldots , f_ n)$ be a finitely generated ideal of $R$. For any $R$-module $N$ the Koszul homology group $H_1(N, f_\bullet )$ defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/05EE" data-tag="05EE">15.91.6</a> is annihilated by $I$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $(x_1, \ldots , x_ n) \in N^{\oplus n}$ with $f_ i x_ j = f_ j x_ i$. Then we have $f_ i(x_1, \ldots , x_ n) = (f_ i x_ i, \ldots , f_ i x_ n)$. In other words $f_ i$ annihilates $H_1(N, f_\bullet )$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>